## Starting or adopting a project

Any project worth more than one session keeps a logbook. When starting a new
project, or when asked to set up a repository that has no `bitacora.config.json`,
follow the `start-project` skill before writing feature code.

Where a `bitacora.config.json` already exists: the logs are not `@`-imported, so
read them on demand — `node .bitacora/cli.mjs recall <tag>` before touching an
unfamiliar or risky area, and log mistakes the moment they happen rather than at
the end of the session.
